d mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T07:44:52-07:00","id":277224,"title":"","content":"pretty much that.<br /> <br /> <br /> In Modern New York I'd have Yu Brothers Accounting and Law, LLC. or something similar back in the 1800's.<br /> <br /> In Exalted I already use an entertainment complex (everything from gateway/go to the depravities of the rich and jaded) called The Cathouse in Nexus that does this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Depending on how many students are being trained and if they live out of the building or not you might need a business with a lot of traffic to help cover up arrivals and departures, but that's about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T01:05:15-07:00","id":278652,"title":"","content":"At least in New York, I'd hide it in play sight: <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://cdn2.holytaco.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/10/fat-ninja.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>CHAZ DINKERMAN'S SHADOW NINJA SCHOOL</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\">Have you ever wanted to be a <b>real ninja warrior</b>? Have you wanted to be a <b>master of disguise</b> or learn how to kill someone in <b>five hundred different ways</b>? Well now, for only <b>$19.99</b> a month, you can!<br /> <br /> Ten years ago, Chaz Dinkerman discovered a <b>lost ninja temple</b> while backpacking through Japan. There he managed to convince the <b>ancient and esteemed masters</b> to teach him their techniques - techniques which he is now willing to pass on to you!<br /> <br /> Within less than <b>six months</b> you will learn a variety of useful grappling techniques, punches, kicks and the basics of over <b>nine different martial arts</b> includeing karate, aikido, jujitsu, bushido and, of course, ninjutsu, all taught by <b>world renowned combat master</b> Chaz Dinkerman himself.<br /> <br /> Chaz will also teach you the secrets of <b>ninja stealth</b>, which will allow you to hide yourself. <b>Ninja disguise</b> techniques, <b>Ninja swimming</b> methods and even the dreaded <b>One Touch Secret Ninja Death Attack</b>, an ability so fearsome that Chaz has sworn to never use it again! Still, if he decides you are worthy, or for a one time fee of <b>$99.99</b> he will teach you the basics of this ultimate offensive tool, one which you must swear to only ever use in a life or death situation!<br /> <br /> Chaz Dinkerman's Shadow Ninja School is open from Noon-8pm, Monday through Friday.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Plaster some badly drawn pictures of ninja on the front of the building, or even better, some anime ninja characters like Naruto to make it perfect.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, who the hell would ever think that Chaz Dinkerman's Shadow Ninja School actually has <i>real</i> ninja there. Can you imagine how the conversation of trying to convince someone would go?","sig